#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""make_claims_check.py — our article, claim by claim, with the passages of the cited PDFs that support each claim.

What it does. For every sentence (or table cell) of the article that cites a paper, it cuts the supporting
passage out of YOUR OWN copy of that paper's PDF, as it is printed on the page, and highlights the words.
It adds what we cite the paper for, whether the paper supports it completely, and whether the paper says
it firsthand. Everything else in this file is our own text and the positions of the passages on the pages
(page numbers and boxes); no text of any cited paper is stored in it.

Run (the folder of the repository is ~/dmt-phiid unless you give another one):
    python3 make_claims_check.py
    python3 make_claims_check.py /path/to/dmt-phiid

Needs pdftoppm (Ubuntu package poppler-utils). Reads the PDFs in external/papers/. A PDF it needs that is only in
~/Downloads/new_papers/ it first copies into external/papers/ (it never replaces a file there), and it takes Vasa2018_SI.pdf
out of Vasa2018_SI.zip. Writes external/claims_check/index.html and its images; external/ is ignored by git, so
nothing it writes can enter the repository.
"""
